{"tool_name":"cvmatch_template","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>It implements the template matching function from the&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.google.com/url?q=http%3A%2F%2Fopencv.willowgarage.com%2Fwiki%2FWelcome&amp;sa=D&amp;sntz=1&amp;usg=AFrqEzcCNHnJ0fdYSuCF8-zkEDPTmXHM6Q\">OpenCV</a>&nbsp;library. The java interface of OpenCV was done through the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/bytedeco/javacv\">javacv</a>&nbsp;library. It is quite similar as the existing&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.google.com/url?q=http%3A%2F%2Frsbweb.nih.gov%2Fij%2Fplugins%2Ftemplate-matching.html&amp;sa=D&amp;sntz=1&amp;usg=AFrqEzctKV83t8lKLLkoZD6XkITV9nO1_w\">template matching plugin</a>&nbsp;but runs much faster and users could choose among six matching methods:&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>1.Squared difference</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>2.Normalized squared difference</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>3.Cross-correlation</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>4.Normalized cross-correlation</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>5.Correlation coefficient</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>6.Normalized correlation coefficient</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>The detailed algorithms could be found&nbsp;<a href=\"https://docs.opencv.org/2.4/doc/tutorials/imgproc/histograms/template_matching/template_matching.html\">here</a>.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>The cvMatch_Template will search a specific object (image pattern) over an image of interest by the user-specified method.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>","summary":"","value":"<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>It implements the template matching function from the&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.google.com/url?q=http%3A%2F%2Fopencv.willowgarage.com%2Fwiki%2FWelcome&amp;sa=D&amp;sntz=1&amp;usg=AFrqEzcCNHnJ0fdYSuCF8-zkEDPTmXHM6Q\">OpenCV</a>&nbsp;library. The java interface of OpenCV was done through the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/bytedeco/javacv\">javacv</a>&nbsp;library. It is quite similar as the existing&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.google.com/url?q=http%3A%2F%2Frsbweb.nih.gov%2Fij%2Fplugins%2Ftemplate-matching.html&amp;sa=D&amp;sntz=1&amp;usg=AFrqEzctKV83t8lKLLkoZD6XkITV9nO1_w\">template matching plugin</a>&nbsp;but runs much faste